 "model": {
  "alpha": 0.05,
  "description": "n independent units (held-out questions, or families). Each unit is a win (the tuned model hits at 5, the base model misses) with probability w, a loss (the tuned model misses, the base model hits) with probability l, or a tie with probability t = 1 - w - l. The exact sign test drops the ties; with d discordant units of which k are wins and X ~ Binomial(d, 1/2), the two-sided p-value is min(1, 2 * min(P(X <= k), P(X >= k))) and the one-sided p-value is P(X >= k), both exact fractions, and the test rejects when p <= alpha. Power is the exact multinomial probability of a rejection in the tuned model's favour (k > d - k).",
  "n_max": 400,
  "notes": {
   "family_units": "units are families, a family's sign being that of its summed per-question differences in hit at 5 (ties dropped); w_f is the family-level win probability, l_f = 0",
   "min_w_at_n": "the smallest w on the grid 0.01, 0.02, ... (l = loss_ratio * w, w + l <= 1) whose power at n reaches target_power; null if none does",
   "n_for_power": "first_n: the smallest n whose power reaches target_power; stable_n: the smallest n from which the power stays at or above it for every n up to n_max; null when not reached. Exact power is saw-toothed in n, so the two can differ"
  },
  "rounding": "floats rounded to 4 decimal places",
  "target_power": 0.8,
  "w_grid_step": 0.01
 },
